# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: reader-printer-vendor-divergences -- READ / PRIN1 cases where AutoCAD and BricsCAD differ, or both differ from clautolisp, not modelled yet
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: windows-runner-sunset-probe-campaign
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-28

Measured by the sunset campaign's B3 probe (probe-reader-printer.lsp,
2026-10-28: AutoCAD 2022 job 17540963671, BricsCAD V25 Windows 17540963675,
V26 macOS 17540963672); the full table is in the spec's READ / PRIN1
"Tested Behaviour". Fixed in 2.3.76: exponent reals without a dot, octal
escapes, unknown escapes dropping the backslash, PRIN1's control-character
escapes. Left:

1. BOTH products, clautolisp differs: READ ".5" is an error (AutoCAD
   "misplaced dot", BricsCAD syntax error); clautolisp reads 0.5 (a
   regression test, strict-real-accepts-dot-with-digits-on-either-side,
   asserts it, from a SCHMS literal "42." -- which stays a real on both).
   Decide: follow the products (READ and LOAD alike?) or keep the leniency
   and warn. The probe measured READ only: measure LOAD of a file holding
   (setq x .5) first.
2. Per product, to model behind the dialect:
   - "+.5" / "-.5": AutoCAD the symbol + / -, BricsCAD the symbol +.5;
   - "1.5.2": AutoCAD the symbol 1, BricsCAD 1.5.2 (clautolisp's);
   - "a.b": AutoCAD A (and "(a.b)" is (A)), BricsCAD A.B (clautolisp's);
   - a block comment before the token: (read ";| c |; 3") is 3 on
     AutoCAD, nil on BricsCAD (clautolisp's);
   - "\u0041": AutoCAD "uu0041", BricsCAD "U0041" (clautolisp "u0041");
   - "\0": AutoCAD ends the string, BricsCAD gives two NULs;
   - PRIN1 of an astral character: AutoCAD \000 (its code page).
